{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: kernel K2, K3 and K11 at exact head 51d24df8af24891fe3036c2750fc664071eebe82, tree de5c4b3f10b9fa481f86c99b3233f92c5fc7dac9 (review request df8054f4, promise f2c764ca, implementation 30c7c3ec / 79ee2bae). There are two documentation findings; F1 is required. I found no code defect. The moves, the boundary check and the evidence pass my checks. A successor that changes only docs/kernel.md and notes/ needs no new gate (docs/testing.md:597). Approval also needs the planner's ruling on the scoped continuation for this head, which is not yet given.\n\nRead order: I read the primary, notes/implementation/2026-10-24-kernel-hygiene.md (artifact ce79699c), first and in full. Then I read docs/kernel.md, scripts/check-kernel-boundary.mjs and its test, the evidence index, the gate and continuation receipts (306f0211, 0a5dd2b0, 3e2711cd and fb719719), and the full tree diff from Main e63b2a7b.\n\nF1 (required). docs/kernel.md gives status that is already wrong at this head, and would be wrong on Main after landing. Lines 14, 106, 127 and 290 say that the ordinary gate and the exact-head checker review \"remain pending\". Line 78 says \"K11 implemented; review pending\", and line 184 says \"final review remains pending\". The ordinary gate has run and failed at 8658d109, and the scoped continuations have passed. Once this head lands, \"review pending\" is false. The design-note status convention (sweep 25323213) asks for status that matches Main, with review-pending wording dropped in the landing head itself. Requested fix: in docs/kernel.md only, use wording that stays true once this head lands. For example: \"K2, K3 and K11 are implemented by request 30c7c3ec. The implementation report records the checks, the failed gate at 8658d109 and its scoped continuations.\" The dated implementation note may keep its own pending lines.\n\nF2 (same successor, documentation). docs/kernel.md section 7 counts \"adds a file or an export to packages/contract, packages/derive, or the kernel part of packages/bytes\" as adding to the kernel. This head does that in two places, both as relocations:\n- derive gains packages/derive/src/field-types.ts and the export \"./field-types\". fieldAssignable is a grammar rule of field types that derive's validator already relied on, and derive already re-exported it (validate/fields.ts:26 at Main). It now lives where the validator lives, which is what K2 asks.\n- bytes gains \"export type { Signer }\" in src/index.ts. Signer is defined in bytes/src/signer.ts, in the signature domain that is kernel. Before, it was exposed only through bytes/application, which has moved out. The export is type-only, and the platform codecs need it.\nIn my view neither can be a platform service. A field-type rule must sit with the derivation that judges fields. A signer type belongs with the signature functions that bytes owns. Please name both additions in the note or in section 5 (K2 and K3), with this reason. Then the record matches the rule, and the request's \"adds nothing to the kernel\" is read as \"adds no new kernel capability\".\n\nMoves only (request 30c7c3ec). I compared every modified or renamed file outside notes/ and docs/ with Main e63b2a7b, with module specifiers masked. All 20 codec modules, validate-package.ts, field-types.ts and the eight moved test files differ from their Main bodies only in import specifiers. The exception is platform/test/package-graph.test.ts, which splits one import line into two. The other differences are all expected:\n- package manifests and exports;\n- the four tsconfig files, which add only the dap-platform/application and application-v2 paths (the rest is reformatting, semantically equal);\n- the release plan and its test;\n- active-source.test.mjs;\n- one diagnostic origin label in definition-corpus/bytes-fixtures.ts, which is not part of any pinned digest;\n- the seven seal values;\n- the root test script, which now runs the boundary check;\n- the bytes Signer export above, and the removal of validate-package from derive's index.\nNo live importer of the old codec or validate-package paths remains. The only matches are in the historical rename records, scripts/rename-workspaces.mjs and workspace-rename-preservation.json. Package validation has no caller in packages/replay or the scope runtime, so promise 9 (section 6) is unaffected.\n\nPlacement, citing docs/kernel.md section 7.\n- K2: production derive no longer imports package-graph. package-graph is now a devDependency of derive, for the corpus only.\n- K3: packages/bytes/src holds no application file.\n- K11: examples/demo-repo is gone, and docs/policy-pack.md replaces its command and link with one sentence.\n- The boundary check: I ran `node scripts/check-kernel-boundary.mjs` in a scratch export of this head. It reports 124 production sources and 0 refusals. I repeated the paired control there, uncommitted. A temporary `import \"@generalbusiness/dap-platform\"` in derive/src/index.ts gave \"packages/derive/src/index.ts: forbidden workspace edge @generalbusiness/dap-platform\". A temporary package-graph import in bytes/src/index.ts gave the same refusal, naming bytes. Restoring each file returned 0 refusals.\n- The approved-library table lists exactly @noble/curves 2.4.0, @noble/hashes 2.4.0 and jsonata 2.2.2, which matches ruling 9ed512c0.\n\nGate and continuation, as recorded and checked.\n- Raw stages/test.log of gate 306f0211 at 8658d109 (tree 635e6cb7): \"Test Files 4 failed | 489 passed | 1 skipped (494)\", \"Tests 2 failed | 3509 passed | 3 skipped (3514)\". The four failed files are:\n  - the two Lending suites, which fail to load with ENOTDIR at …/platform/src/index.ts/application. This is the alias defect in my c4298a28. Nine Lending cases are absent.\n  - replay archive-git-v2-layout.test.ts, where the local gitSource verification at line 108 returned archive-failure instead of consistent after 10,021 ms;\n  - scope floor-archive.test.ts, where