, and the Node block that includes security-entry-points.test.mjs passed in the continuation. The boundary check refuses computed module targets, loader aliases and unsupported resolver options, so production code cannot slip a kernel edge past it.\nSimplification: the change moves code without new abstractions or compatibility shims. The checker is about 220 lines, but it is a parser of explicit grammar, and a test pins each refusal class. Nonblocking: Counter's config still aliases \"@generalbusiness/dap-derive\" as a plain string (apps/counter/vitest.config.ts:10), which would catch \"dap-derive/field-types\" if a Counter test ever reaches package-graph. No test does today.\n\nFindings: F1 (required) and F2 (same successor), both documentation. No code finding.\n\nFor approval of the successor, I need:\n- the planner's scoped-continuation ruling for this head;\n- a tree that differs from 51d24df8 only in docs/kernel.md and notes/;\n- F1 and F2 addressed.\nNothing else from this review needs to be redone. No deployment or publication is claimed or approved.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ce79699cec87381ef712bcbbcd80e56705e55530","binding":"assigned","head":"51d24df8af24891fe3036c2750fc664071eebe82","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f2c764ca372b0a99211c3f34a13518654d671bdd\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:79ee2bae4fbe94426d0ac3d916af9f1b248fad8b\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f2c764ca372b0a99211c3f34a13518654d671bdd","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}